Counterparty risk can be illustrated using a derivatives transaction between two counterparties. If one of them is in a net gain (“winning”) position, the other is in a net loss (“losing”) position. The position that is losing may simply *refuse to pay and fulfill its obligations.* This risk also includes #voir("settlement-risk").

It is a subtype of #voir("credit-risk").
